---@class scaleway.lb_zoned_v1.HealthCheck
---@field port? number Port to use for the backend server health check.
---@field check_delay? number Time to wait between two consecutive health checks. (in milliseconds)
---@field check_timeout? number Maximum time a backend server has to reply to the health check. (in milliseconds)
---@field check_max_retries? number Number of consecutive unsuccessful health checks after which the server will be considered dead.
---@field tcp_config? any|distilled.Null Object to configure a basic TCP health check. Precisely one of tcp_config, mysql_config, pgsql_config, ldap_config, redis_config, http_config, https_config can be set.
---@field mysql_config? scaleway.lb_zoned_v1.HealthCheckMysqlConfig|distilled.Null Object to configure a MySQL health check. The check requires MySQL >=3.22 or <9.0. For older or newer versions, use a TCP health check. Precisely one of tcp_config, mysql_config, pgsql_config, ldap_config, redis_config, http_config, https_config can be set.
---@field pgsql_config? scaleway.lb_zoned_v1.HealthCheckPgsqlConfig|distilled.Null Object to configure a PostgreSQL health check. Precisely one of tcp_config, mysql_config, pgsql_config, ldap_config, redis_config, http_config, https_config can be set.
---@field ldap_config? any|distilled.Null Object to configure an LDAP health check. The response is analyzed to find the LDAPv3 response message. Precisely one of tcp_config, mysql_config, pgsql_config, ldap_config, redis_config, http_config, https_config can be set.
---@field redis_config? any|distilled.Null Object to configure a Redis health check. The response is analyzed to find the +PONG response message. Precisely one of tcp_config, mysql_config, pgsql_config, ldap_config, redis_config, http_config, https_config can be set.
---@field http_config? scaleway.lb_zoned_v1.HealthCheckHttpConfig|distilled.Null Object to configure an HTTP health check. Precisely one of tcp_config, mysql_config, pgsql_config, ldap_config, redis_config, http_config, https_config can be set.
---@field https_config? scaleway.lb_zoned_v1.HealthCheckHttpsConfig|distilled.Null Object to configure an HTTPS health check. Precisely one of tcp_config, mysql_config, pgsql_config, ldap_config, redis_config, http_config, https_config can be set.
---@field check_send_proxy? boolean Defines whether proxy protocol should be activated for the health check.
---@field transient_check_delay? string|distilled.Null Time to wait between two consecutive health checks when a backend server is in a transient state (going UP or DOWN). (in seconds)

---@class scaleway.lb_zoned_v1.HealthCheckHttpConfig
---@field uri? string HTTP path used for the health check. The HTTP path to use when performing a health check on backend servers.
---@field method? string HTTP method used for the health check. The HTTP method used when performing a health check on backend servers.
---@field code? number|distilled.Null HTTP response code expected for a successful health check. The HTTP response code that should be returned for a health check to be considered successful.
---@field host_header? string HTTP host header used for the health check. The HTTP host header used when performing a health check on backend servers.

---@class scaleway.lb_zoned_v1.HealthCheckHttpsConfig
